00:50:47.471 --> 00:50:48.304
Yeah.

00:50:48.304 --> 00:50:49.437
And those are fun.

00:50:49.437 --> 00:50:50.275
Those stories are fun,

00:50:50.275 --> 00:50:52.624
but also that that kinda
conversation can be fun,

00:50:52.624 --> 00:50:54.457
but I think especially

00:50:55.385 --> 00:50:56.891
when you're talking about something

00:50:56.891 --> 00:50:59.808
that you have a disagreement about.

00:51:02.456 --> 00:51:05.270
There's a concept that I heard
somebody described one time,

00:51:05.270 --> 00:51:06.999
what typically happens online,

00:51:06.999 --> 00:51:09.232
which is the straw man,

00:51:09.232 --> 00:51:11.999
which is, you mischaracterize
someone's argument

00:51:11.999 --> 00:51:15.692
and you distill it down to
something that you can easily

00:51:15.692 --> 00:51:16.525
Burn down.

00:51:16.525 --> 00:51:18.334
Take out, yeah.

00:51:18.334 --> 00:51:20.272
But the opposite of that,

00:51:20.272 --> 00:51:23.070
I think is called iron manning?

00:51:23.070 --> 00:51:24.022
I don't know,

00:51:24.022 --> 00:51:25.012
something like that.

00:51:25.012 --> 00:51:26.151
Okay.

00:51:26.151 --> 00:51:27.133
But it's like,

00:51:27.133 --> 00:51:32.050
I'm going to understand and be
able to state your position,

00:51:35.252 --> 00:51:38.891
in the most defensible
way I can think of, right?

00:51:38.891 --> 00:51:41.052
I'm gonna give you the
benefit of the doubt,

00:51:41.052 --> 00:51:46.052
I'm gonna try to capture the
essence of what you're saying

00:51:46.574 --> 00:51:48.353
in a way that you can agree with.

00:51:48.353 --> 00:51:50.504
So that then when I disagree with it,

00:51:50.504 --> 00:51:52.312
you can hear my disagreement,

00:51:52.312 --> 00:51:54.684
because you know you've been heard.

00:51:54.684 --> 00:51:56.101
Yeah, but also,

00:51:57.655 --> 00:52:00.119
there's just something about

00:52:00.119 --> 00:52:04.612
just making yourself willing
to go through the process

00:52:04.612 --> 00:52:08.324
of being like, okay, before I
just go into my talking points

00:52:08.324 --> 00:52:10.754
and break out my ideology,

00:52:10.754 --> 00:52:12.754
I am going to understand

00:52:15.121 --> 00:52:16.059
and be able to say things like,

00:52:16.059 --> 00:52:17.281
"So you're saying,

00:52:17.281 --> 00:52:18.938
if I'm hearing you correctly,

00:52:18.938 --> 00:52:20.384
you're saying this, this and this

00:52:20.384 --> 00:52:21.217
and they say no,

00:52:21.217 --> 00:52:22.186
that's not what I'm saying."

00:52:22.186 --> 00:52:23.565
Keep listening.

00:52:23.565 --> 00:52:24.398
Mm-hmm.
And then if you can

00:52:24.398 --> 00:52:25.231
finally get to

00:52:25.231 --> 00:52:26.858
your saying this and this,

00:52:26.858 --> 00:52:28.338
yes.

00:52:28.338 --> 00:52:30.248
Even if you disagree,

00:52:30.248 --> 00:52:31.859
there's progress that's been made.

00:52:31.859 --> 00:52:33.005
There's some kind of common ground

00:52:33.005 --> 00:52:34.375
'cause you've at least agreed

00:52:34.375 --> 00:52:36.435
to have a rational
conversation about something.

00:52:36.435 --> 00:52:37.268
Yeah.

